# Trivy Ignore File
# This file contains CVEs that are intentionally ignored during security scans

# CVE-2026-56854: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: source-address restriction silently ignored
#   for Permissions returned by non-public-key auth callbacks
# Severity: CRITICAL (Trivy/NVD). GitHub Advisory GHSA-gjhq-gjfw-99mq rates it HIGH
#   with CVSS 3.1 7.5 (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N)
# Affected: golang.org/x/crypto v0.52.0 embedded in usr/local/bin/op (1Password CLI 2.39.0)
# Fixed in: golang.org/x/crypto 0.55.0
# Reason: 1Password CLI is a closed-source pre-built binary. 2.39.0 is the latest release
#   (confirmed 2026-09-08 via https://app-updates.agilebits.com/check/1/0/CLI2/en/0/N,
#   the same endpoint update-dev-tools.yml polls), so there is no version to upgrade to.
#   The defect is in the *server* side of x/crypto/ssh: a source-address critical option
#   set by PasswordCallback / KeyboardInteractiveCallback / NoClientAuthCallback /
#   GSSAPIWithMICConfig.AllowLogin was not checked against the client's remote address.
#   op is used here as a client-side secrets CLI and does not expose an SSH server in
#   this image, so the vulnerable code path is not reachable in our usage.
# Expected resolution: Wait for 1Password to ship a CLI build with x/crypto >= 0.55.0.
#   update-dev-tools.yml bumps OP_CLI_VERSION automatically; remove this entry once a
#   scan after that bump no longer reports CVE-2026-56854.
# Tracking: https://developer.1password.com/docs/cli/release-notes/
# Note 2026-09-08: Advisory published 2026-08-28. main's Trivy scan has failed since
#   2026-09-01 (last success 2026-08-31), which matches the Trivy DB picking this up.
# Review date: 2026-11-08
CVE-2026-56854

# CVE-2026-102992: piscina: Prototype-pollution gadget in ThreadPool.options allows RCE
# Severity: CRITICAL (Trivy/NVD); upstream advisory rates it HIGH
# Affected: piscina 4.9.3 bundled in Cursor CLI 2026.10.01-e373342
# Fixed in: piscina 4.9.4, 5.3.2, 6.0.0-rc.5
# Reason: Cursor's official installer still distributes this version (checked 2026-10-05).
#   Verified piscina/package.json in its linux/x64 archive; no newer official CLI build
#   is offered by the installer. Updating npm/global.json cannot replace this private
#   dependency. Temporarily accept the finding while awaiting a patched Cursor bundle.
# Risk: Exploitation requires another bug to pollute Object.prototype in the CLI process;
#   then worker options can execute code or inject environment variables. We have not
#   proven that prerequisite unreachable in Cursor. This exception does not fix the RCE.
# Expected resolution: Recheck the official bundle and remove this entry once it ships
#   a patched piscina version. This plain-text ignore applies to this CVE image-wide
#   and does not expire automatically; review any additional occurrences at that time.
# Tracking: https://github.com/keito4/config/issues/1334
# Advisory: https://github.com/piscinajs/piscina/security/advisories/GHSA-67c8-pqhq-4rmx
# Installer: https://cursor.com/install
# Review date: 2026-11-05
CVE-2026-102992

# CVE-2026-102828: simple-git: critical vulnerability (Trivy CRITICAL)
# CVE-2026-102829: @simple-git/argv-parser: critical vulnerability (Trivy CRITICAL)
# Severity: CRITICAL
# Affected: simple-git 3.36.0 / @simple-git/argv-parser 1.1.1
#   (usr/local/lib/node_modules/difit/node_modules/)
# Fixed in: simple-git 4.0.1 / @simple-git/argv-parser 2.0.1
# Reason: difit declares simple-git ^3.28.0 and has no release supporting simple-git 4.x,
#   so updating npm/global.json cannot pull the fix. An npm override would force a major
#   bump into difit untested. Temporarily accept while waiting for difit to support 4.x.
# Risk: difit is a local diff viewer run by the developer against their own repositories;
#   untrusted git arguments are not passed to it in this image. This exception does not fix it.
# Expected resolution: Remove these entries once difit depends on simple-git >= 4.0.1.
# Tracking: https://github.com/keito4/config/issues/1339
# Note 2026-10-10: Accepted per owner decision in monthly maintenance (C).
# Review date: 2026-11-10
CVE-2026-102828
CVE-2026-102829
